msgctxt "Languages::ee_first_purchase_verivication_instructions"
msgid "<p>This add-on adds the <strong>Customer's first purchase</strong> condition to cart promotions.</p><ol><li>Open <strong>Marketing -> Promotions</strong> and create or edit a cart promotion.</li><li>Add a condition and choose <strong>Customer's first purchase</strong>.</li><li>The condition is fulfilled only for signed-in customers without previous orders. Incomplete orders are ignored.</li><li>In CS-Cart Ultimate the check is performed inside the current storefront. In Multi-Vendor the check is performed across the marketplace.</li></ol>"
msgstr ""
"<h4>Add-on purpose</h4>"
"<p>The add-on extends CS-Cart promotions and requires the <strong>Reward points</strong> add-on. It provides two independent features: a <strong>first purchase bonus</strong> through a promotion condition and <strong>increased reward points for campaigns</strong> through a separate cart promotion bonus.</p>"
"<h4>1. First purchase bonus</h4>"
"<p>For this feature, the add-on adds the <strong>Customer's first purchase</strong> promotion condition. The condition is available in catalog and cart promotions. The condition itself does not grant points or discounts; it only checks that the signed-in customer has no previous orders. Incomplete orders are ignored.</p>"
"<p>How to use it: create a catalog or cart promotion, add the <strong>Customer's first purchase</strong> condition, then add a standard promotion bonus: product discount, order discount, free shipping, coupon, or another bonus available for the selected promotion type. In CS-Cart Ultimate the check is limited to the current storefront. In Multi-Vendor the customer's order history is checked across the marketplace.</p>"
"<h4>2. Reward points for campaigns</h4>"
"<p>For this feature, the add-on adds the <strong>Reward points: target percent of matching products</strong> cart promotion bonus. This bonus is available only in cart promotions because Reward points calculates and stores points at cart and order level. It is intentionally not shown in catalog promotions.</p>"
"<p>The bonus sets the final reward points percentage for products that match product-scoped promotion conditions. The value is a target percentage, not an extra percentage added on top. If Reward points globally grants 1% and a campaign must grant 5%, enter <strong>5</strong>; matching products will grant 5%.</p>"
"<p>The add-on does not grant points directly. It changes cart reward calculation, then the standard Reward points add-on stores the calculated points in the order. Points are actually credited when the order is moved to a status where reward points granting is enabled, for example <strong>Completed</strong>.</p>"
"<h4>Matching products</h4>"
"<p>The add-on uses only product-scoped promotion conditions to select individual products: <strong>Products</strong>, <strong>Categories</strong>, and <strong>Feature</strong>. For a brand campaign, add the <strong>Feature</strong> condition, select the <strong>Brand</strong> feature, and choose the required brand variants.</p>"
"<p>Other conditions, such as first purchase, user group, coupon, order subtotal, country, or shipping method, control whether the whole promotion applies, but they do not select individual products for percentage calculation.</p>"
"<p>If a cart promotion has no <strong>Products</strong>, <strong>Categories</strong>, or <strong>Feature</strong> conditions, the percent bonus applies to all cart products. If several percent bonuses match the same product, the highest target percentage is used.</p>"
"<h4>Examples</h4>"
"<ol><li><strong>First purchase bonus:</strong> create a promotion, add the <strong>Customer's first purchase</strong> condition, and add the required standard bonus, for example product discount or order discount.</li><li><strong>1% for all purchases:</strong> configure the global rule in Reward points; no promotion is required.</li><li><strong>5% by category:</strong> create a cart promotion, add the <strong>Categories</strong> condition, select the category, and add the <strong>Reward points: target percent of matching products</strong> bonus with value <strong>5</strong>.</li><li><strong>5% by brand:</strong> create a cart promotion, add the <strong>Feature</strong> condition, select <strong>Brand</strong> and brand variants, and add the bonus with value <strong>5</strong>.</li></ol>"
